  "description": "RAGSEB crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C60 H118 Eu3 Mn7 N6 O41,3(C2 H3 N1). From the CIF bond table, Eu1 (Eu) has 9 O neighbors; Eu2 (Eu) has 9 O neighbors; Eu3 (Eu) has 9 O neighbors; Mn1 (Mn) has 6 O neighbors; Mn2 (Mn) has 5 O neighbors; Mn3 (Mn) has 5 O neighbors; Mn4 (Mn) has 4 O neighbors; Mn5 (Mn) has 6 O neighbors; Mn6 (Mn) has 6 O neighbors; Mn7 (Mn) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 24 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.002-3.954 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 83.69-130.18°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C66H127Mn7N9Eu3O41. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 3 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
